# Insert-mode Ctrl-T indents the line and keeps the cursor on the same
# TEXT: Neovim wi<C-t>X<Esc> on "foo bar" -> "<indent>foo Xbar". mnml
# leaves the cursor at the old column, so X lands inside the indent.
write f.txt "foo bar\n"
open f.txt
command editor.use_vim
key w
key i
key ctrl+t
type X
key esc
ex w
expect file f.txt contains "foo Xbar"
